What do you mean, 'They're not cursed'?  They bloody well are cursed.  Most
of the items in the ghost pile, anyway.

There are a number of ways to un-curse an item.

	1) Dipping the item in a potion of holy water.  This only
works on one item, and is rather a waste of a highly useful item, imho.

	2) Reading a blessed scroll of remove curse will uncurse all
the items in your inventory, whether you are wielding the item or not.
This is the best way to go, again imho.

	3) Zapping the item with a wand of cancellation, which has the
usually unhealthy side effect of cancelling *all* the enchantments on
the item (except the name of the item, if it's a named weapon.)  That
means that potions will be turned to water, scrolls will be erased,
and armor and weapons will be made +0.

